module bindings.rust.session_auth_state_owner_binding_missing;

// A multi-step login keeps its progress in an authentication state bound to
// the session: the first request that names a principal creates the state,
// and every later request on that session resolves it again by the session
// key alone. The request also names the principal its own credential is
// verified against, and the verified credential is credited to the resolved
// state -- so unless the state's owner is compared with the principal the
// request names, one account's valid credential completes another account's
// login. The account the state was created for is the account that gets
// authorized when the state verifies.
//
// The auth-state API publishes every atom of the flow this recognises:
// get_auth_state_for_request resolves the state through the session for a
// request-named principal, validate_credential verifies a credential for a
// named principal, and add_valid_credential credits the verified credential
// to the state. AuthState::username is the owner read. What is matched here
// is the login function that performs all three steps while never reading
// the state's owner. The atoms are the API's own names, present in every
// revision, and the owner read is the idiom the OTP login and the SSO login
// already use to bind the state's owner to the principal they name.
//
// The judgement lives in the pack rule; this binding only recognises the
// atoms. Every clause is an exact call token over the consuming function's
// own context, so prose in a comment satisfies neither side and an owner
// read in a sibling function does not clear the login.
//
// Within one codebase the shape is rare by construction: a protocol
// implementation that resolves its state through the session, verifies a
// request-named principal's credential and credits it to that state has
// exactly one function per login method, and any login method that binds
// the owner -- by validating against the state's own username or by
// comparing the two -- is not matched.

binding sessionAuthStateOwnerBindingMissing {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "rust" and node.context.call in ["get_auth_state_for_request"] and node.context.call in ["validate_credential"] and node.context.call in ["add_valid_credential"] and not (node.context.call in ["username"])
  emit issue code.SessionAuthStateOwnerBindingMissing at node
}
